media: v4l2-core: name a registered sensor clock after the device

__devm_v4l2_sensor_clk_get() registers a fixed-rate clock itself when the
platform supplies none, which is the normal case on ACPI. It names that
clock after the con_id the caller passed. Clock names are global, so a
board carrying two identical sensors has both of them register the same
name, and the second one to probe fails with -EEXIST and never binds.

The Chuwi Vi8 Plus is such a board: two ov2680, both asking for "xvclk".
Which one loses is decided by probe order and changes between boots, and
on an atomisp machine it costs both cameras rather than one, because the
video nodes are created from the async notifier's .complete callback and
that never fires while an expected subdev is missing.

The name is only needed to identify the clock, which is handed straight
back to the caller rather than looked up by name, so deriving it from the
device makes it unique without affecting anything else. The function
already does exactly that when the caller passes no con_id; do it for the
registration in every case, and keep using the con_id for the lookup that
precedes it.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
---
 Generated against the Ubuntu linux-source-7.0.0 tree (7.0.0-34-generic).
 Apply with: git am, or patch -p1 < this file

 Status: the mechanism is verified on the reference unit, this exact hunk
 is not. Making ov2680 pass NULL as its con_id takes the same branch and
 produces the same per-device clock name; with that change both sensors
 bound on every attempt and /dev/video0 appeared. The hunk below moves
 that behaviour into the helper, where it also covers sensors that have a
 reason to keep their con_id, and it has not itself been compiled.
---
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-common.c
@@ -792,14 +792,17 @@
 	/* We need a rate to create a clock. */
 	if (ret)
 		return ERR_PTR(ret == -EINVAL ? -EPROBE_DEFER : ret);
 
-	if (!id) {
-		clk_id = kasprintf(GFP_KERNEL, "clk-%s", dev_name(dev));
-		if (!clk_id)
-			return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
-		id = clk_id;
-	}
+	/*
+	 * The clock is registered here rather than looked up, so its name only
+	 * has to be unique -- and it has to be: two identical sensors on one
+	 * board would otherwise both register the caller's con_id, and the
+	 * second would fail to probe with -EEXIST.
+	 */
+	clk_id = kasprintf(GFP_KERNEL, "clk-%s", dev_name(dev));
+	if (!clk_id)
+		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 
-	clk_hw = devm_clk_hw_register_fixed_rate(dev, id, NULL, 0, rate);
+	clk_hw = devm_clk_hw_register_fixed_rate(dev, clk_id, NULL, 0, rate);
 	if (IS_ERR(clk_hw))
 		return ERR_CAST(clk_hw);
 
